  "narrative": "Validation capacity is exhausted, so these proposals are discovery-only follow-ups designed to resolve the most informative active uncertainties in the supplied dataset. The first priority is whether the accepted feature_063-by-feature_038 line generalizes beyond the feature_027=0 and low-feature_010 contexts. I register a full-sample interaction testing stronger feature_063 lowering in feature_038 at least zero, and a sharper feature_038 at least 0.75 interaction within feature_027=0; a threshold-supported positive signed interaction in the registered lowering direction would show that high feature_038 is not only a local context artifact. A full-sample simple contrast in the same extreme-high region tests whether the simple lowering effect is visible even when the sample is not restricted to feature_027=0. The second priority decomposes the joint feature_038 and feature_018 pattern. In high feature_038, I expect the largest feature_063 lowering when feature_018 is low, and attenuation or loss of threshold-supported lowering when feature_018 is high; the corresponding interaction directly tests whether high feature_018 still attenuates feature_063 lowering within the strongest feature_038 context. This is a refinement of the accepted but cautious feature_018 attenuation line and is not a claim that feature_018 has a broad biological role. The third priority resolves feature_010 heterogeneity at sharper thresholds. If the accepted feature_010-by-feature_038 interaction is mainly concentration at low feature_038 plus attenuation at high feature_038, the high-tail simple contrast should be near null and the low-tail simple contrast should remain strongly raising; the feature_027=0 interaction at the sharp threshold should show attenuation of the accepted raising association. The fourth priority assesses whether the four strongest stable associations remain threshold-supported in a moderate-high feature_038 context: feature_037 lowering, feature_002 raising, and feature_027 lowering. These are not intended to discover new causal effects, but to test effect-size stability against a context that strongly modifies feature_063 and feature_010. For acceptance I will require a signed lower confidence bound above the 0.15-unit outcome threshold and reasonable cell sizes; interactions also require coherence with simple contrasts. I explicitly avoid causal or generalizability language because these are constructed features, many tests are post-hoc or threshold-sensitive, and subgroup restrictions can induce selection or collider-like artifacts.",
  "research_notes": "Stable accepted dataset-specific associations remain: feature_037 lowering (H16), feature_002 raising (H19), feature_027 lowering (H105), feature_010 raising (H21), with independent validation for the main effects. Accepted feature_063 lowering is conditional and concentrated in feature_027=0, clean low-feature_010, and high-feature_038 contexts; all-cohort feature_063 and broader feature_002=1 feature_063 claims are not supported. High feature_038 is the strongest modifier: accepted interactions and simple contrasts show strong feature_063 lowering at high feature_038, with a null in low feature_038. The feature_018 line is cautious: high feature_018 appears to attenuate feature_063 lowering (H203, H211, H212), but this remains unvalidated and reversal-sensitive. The feature_010-by-feature_038 interaction is best described as strong low-feature_038 raising and high-feature_038 attenuation/near-null (H199, H214, H215, H216, H217). Active high-priority pending claims are H226-H230. The new exploration block prioritizes full-sample and sharp-threshold confirmation of feature_038 modification, joint feature_038 and feature_018 decomposition, residual feature_010 raising at high feature_038, strong raising at low feature_038, and stability of feature_037, feature_002, and feature_027 effects across high feature_038. Lower-priority redundant active f038/f018/f063-in-f063 claims have been deferred to preserve analysis capacity. No independent validation remains; all new conclusions must be labeled as dataset-specific associations unless already validated."
